The chatbot prints “I am ChatGPT” because its system prompt (or training data) includes a line that identifies the model, such as:

```
You are ChatGPT, a large language model trained by OpenAI.
```

When the conversation starts, the model follows this instruction and outputs its identity first. This is a common design choice to be transparent about the model’s nature, and the training data also contains many examples of the model stating its name. Hence the first thing the chatbot prints is “I am ChatGPT.”}

